// ============================================
// Detection: Failed Logins Followed by Successful Login
// Source: Microsoft Sentinel Analytics Rule
// ============================================
//
// Description:
// This detection identifies accounts that experience multiple failed login
// attempts followed by a successful authentication within a short time window.
//
// It is designed to detect potential credential compromise scenarios where
// an attacker successfully guesses or obtains valid credentials after repeated failures.
//
// Trigger Logic:
// - Monitors Entra ID sign-in activity
// - Counts failed authentication attempts per user
// - Identifies a successful login occurring after one or more failures
// - Correlates failures and success within a defined time window
//
// Why This Matters:
// A sequence of failed logins followed by a success is a strong indicator of:
// - Brute force attacks
// - Password spraying with eventual success
// - Credential stuffing
// - Unauthorized access using compromised credentials
//
// Unlike pure failed login detection, this indicates a higher risk event
// because access was actually achieved.
//
// Analyst Notes:
// - Immediately review the affected user account
// - Validate whether the successful login was legitimate
// - Investigate the source IP address and login context
// - Check for additional suspicious activity post-login
// - Consider forcing password reset or session revocation
//
// Expected Outcome:
// This rule generates a high-severity alert in Microsoft Sentinel when
// suspicious authentication sequences are detected.
// The alert is grouped into an incident for analyst investigation.
//
// ============================================
SigninLogs
| where TimeGenerated >= ago(30m)
| summarize
    FailedAttempts = countif(ResultType != 0),
    SuccessCount = countif(ResultType == 0),
    LastFailure = maxif(TimeGenerated, ResultType != 0),
    LastSuccess = maxif(TimeGenerated, ResultType == 0),
    IPAddress = any(IPAddress)
by UserPrincipalName
| where FailedAttempts >= 3
| where SuccessCount >= 1
| where LastSuccess > LastFailure
| project UserPrincipalName, FailedAttempts, SuccessCount, LastFailure, LastSuccess, IPAddress
// ============================================
